                                    Chapter I – Objective & Scope of the Project 
 
1.1 Objective of the Project 
 
The primary objective of the CitySamadhan project is to develop a centralized, 
web-based platform that enables citizens to report, track, and manage civic issues 
efficiently. The system aims to bridge the communication gap between citizens and 
municipal authorities by providing a transparent and user-friendly interface for 
complaint registration and resolution. The project focuses on improving the existing 
complaint management process by replacing traditional manual methods with a 
digital solution that ensures accuracy, efficiency, and accountability. It allows users 
to submit complaints related to urban issues such as waste management, road 
damage, water leakage, and public infrastructure problems, along with relevant 
details like images and location. 
1.2 Scope of the Project 
 
The scope of the CitySamadhan system is broad and adaptable, making it suitable 
for implementation in various urban environments. The system is designed as a web
based application that can be accessed from any device with an internet connection, 
ensuring ease of use and accessibility for a wide range of users. The platform 
primarily focuses on enabling citizens to report civic issues and track their resolution 
status. Additionally, it allows authorities to manage complaints efficiently by 
assigning them to relevant departments and updating their status. In conclusion, the 
scope of CitySamadhan extends from basic complaint reporting to creating a 
comprehensive digital ecosystem for civic issue management, with the potential to 
evolve into a smart city solution. 
