Chapter IV – System Analysis & User Requirements 
 
 
4.1 System Analysis 
System analysis is the process of studying the existing system, identifying its 
limitations, and defining the requirements for a new and improved system. In the 
context of civic complaint management, the current systems are largely manual or 
semi-digital, lacking proper tracking, transparency, and efficiency. 
 
The existing methods involve citizens reporting issues through phone calls, emails, 
or physical visits to municipal offices. These approaches are time-consuming, prone 
to errors, and do not provide any mechanism for tracking the status of complaints. 
Additionally, there is no centralized database to store and manage complaints, which 
leads to poor coordination among departments and delayed responses. 
 
The proposed system, CitySamadhan, addresses these limitations by introducing a 
centralized web-based platform. It automates the complaint management process, 
